{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UutGcLfGceNF7EZrddz3C9","type":"tool_result","content":"10:# accessors for it, so the run-status contract — every run (ralph or harden)\n265:# for ralph; provider/model/effort/lenses/rounds for harden). Blank values are\n372:# round (harden round / ralph iteration) and worker/lens summary, preserving the\n770:# the type's stop|steer dot-file basename (`<base>/.harden-stop`, …). Centralises\n771:# the harden/converge pattern of \"look up the signal file, prepend the path\" so\n805:# steer file under root, which the loop's next round consumes (ralph reads\n806:# `.ralph-steer`). Returns 2 when the run is unknown, 3 when its type has no steer\n921:# The hub's New-run flow picks a loop type (ralph|harden), gathers config, and\n927:# collect): ralph takes prd, mode, provider, model, effort, iterations, oversee;\n928:# harden takes target, rounds, lenses, provider, model, effort.\n931:# `almanac` subcommand. ralph config maps to ralph.sh flags; harden launches the\n932:# convergence loop (`harden <target> --loop [--rounds N]`) — its provider/model/\n934:# converge takes goal + exec + rounds + oversee config on argv (the only required\n936:# rides on environment, same shape as harden.\n937:# Returns 1 for an unknown type, 2 when a required field is missing (ralph: prd;\n938:# harden: target; converge: goal+exec).\n963:    ralph)\n965:      printf '%s\\n' ralph\n974:    harden)\n976:      printf '%s\\n%s\\n%s\\n' harden \"$target\" --loop\n979:    converge)\n987:      # Same split as harden: state the runner needs goes on argv (goal, the\n990:      # `almanac converge` — cmd/converge.sh; no launcher hop in this code path.\n991:      # The interactive menu uses almanac_loop_launch converge (the launcher)\n993:      printf '%s\\n' converge\n1010:# beyond its argv. ralph takes all config as flags, so it emits nothing; harden's\n1027:    ralph) : ;;\n1028:    harden)\n1034:    converge)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019Kz3RBNz6eX2dXbntAP8pD","session_id":"19c2339b-02f8-4b81-9b44-59452ec22e33","uuid":"0a87b464-6379-494e-96bd-0358af64cdd2","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:15:35.063Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Find architectural friction in almanac"}
